---
title: Pam Bauer's Banana Bread
description: My old neighbor's banana bread recipe she'd shared with us
tags: midwest
image: https://i0.wp.com/thetimelessbaker.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Sour-Milk-Banana-Bread_-2.jpg?resize=768%2C623&ssl=1
---

Sour milk by adding @vinegar{1/6%tsp}(realistically just a few drops) to @milk{4%tbsp}. Stir to combine then let sit for ~{5%minutes}.

> To create sour milk, the ratio is 1 tbsp white vinegar to 1 cup of milk, so we need approximately 1/16 tbsp here, or just a smidgen more than 1/6 tsp. A few drops is honestly easier.

If using nuts, toast @?nuts{1/2%cup}(walnut preferred, chopped) at 350°F on an ungreased baking pan for ~{6-8%minutes}.

Preheat oven to 325°F.

Cream together @sugar{1%cup}, @brown sugar{1/2%cup}, and @eggs{2}.

Mix in @flour{2%cups}, sour milk, @baking soda{1%tsp}, and @vanilla{1%tsp}.

Add in @butter{1/2%cup}(melted) and @bananas{3}(ripe, mashed).

Grease and flour a #large loaf pan{} and #small loaf pan{}. 

Fill the pans 2/3 full and bake at 325°F. The small loaf will be done after ~{45%minutes}, and the large loaf will be done after another ~{15%minutes}.